<title>GERMANY: Deutsche MG raises Volvo to neutral.</title>
<headline>Deutsche MG raises Volvo to neutral.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German investment house Deutsche MG said on Friday it had raised its recommendation on Swedish auto-maker AB Volvo from &quot;underweight&quot; to &quot;neutral&quot;.</p>
<p>Deutsche MG, a unit of Deutsche Bank AG, said the upgrade was due to what it perceived as the positive trend in Volvo's earnings per share.</p>
<p>Accordingly it raised its 1997 EPS estimate from 9.3 to 16.4 crowns, or to 10.0 crowns per share not including expected capital gains.</p>
<p>For 1998, the bank raised its estimate from 10.9 crowns per share to 13.1 crowns, with nearly no capital gains due.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
